"{\"router\": {\"version\": 1, \"template\": \"\\n{% chat role=\\\"system\\\" %}\\nCarefully read the user query and classify it into exactly one of the following routing decisions:\\n\\n{{reference}} \\u2014 Use when the user wants to search, retrieve, inspect, or identify information from the reference list/bibliography of a specific scientific paper.\\n{{search_arxiv}} \\u2014 Use when the user wants to search for scientific research, papers, or literature on a specific topic, including requests to find relevant papers on arXiv.\\n{{answer}} \\u2014 Use when the query is not primarily a scientific-literature search request, such as general knowledge questions, explanations, summaries, reasoning, or other requests that can be answered directly without searching paper references or arXiv.\\nClassification rules\\nChoose exactly one routing decision.\\nPrioritize the user's primary intent, not individual keywords.\\nIf the user explicitly asks to search the references/bibliography of a paper, choose REFERENCE_SEARCH.\\nIf the user asks to find scientific papers or research about a topic, choose ARXIV_SEARCH.\\nOtherwise, choose ANSWER.\\n\\nAs outtput, return only the selected routing decision. Do not provide an explanation or any additional text.\\n{% endchat %}\\n{%chat role=\\\"user\\\" %}\\nQuery: {{query}}\\n{% endchat %}\\n\", \"description\": \"untested version of the prompt\"}, \"query_expansion\": {\"version\": 1, \"template\": \"\\n    {% chat role=\\\"system\\\" %}\\nToday date: {{date}}\\n        Optimize the following user query by generating up to {{limit}} alternative versions for {{task}} search.\\n\\nRequirements:\\n\\nPreserve the original intent and meaning.\\nIncrease coverage by adding relevant context, synonyms, related concepts, and useful search terms.\\nImprove coherence, clarity, and specificity.\\nEach version should explore a meaningfully different angle while remaining faithful to the original query.\\nAvoid unnecessary verbosity, repetition, or invented assumptions.\\nReturn only the optimized queries as a list.\\nDo not include explanations, labels, numbering, or commentary.\\n{% endchat %}\\n{% chat role=\\\"user\\\" %}\\nInput query:\\n{{query}}\\n{% endchat %}\\n        \", \"description\": \"untested version of the prompt\"}}"